# The wasm-opt arguments for every web module this repository builds: the
# page's start module and the modules split from it, the compute module, and
# the bundles the app SDK writes. One list, so the module a size gate measures
# is the module the site serves.
#
# Read by crates/browser/tilo-browser-runtime/scripts/build.sh,
# crates/browser/tilo-browser-compute/scripts/build.sh and
# crates/dev/tilo-app-cli (embedded when it compiles). A comment is a line
# starting with `#`; every other word is an argument.
-Oz
--enable-bulk-memory
--enable-nontrapping-float-to-int
# The split modules keep the name section the splitter read until it is gone
# with the rest of the debug information, and a producer section buys the page
# nothing.
--strip-debug
--strip-producers
# Sound for rustc's stack-first wasm32 layout: the first KiB is the bottom of
# the stack, reached only by a stack about to overflow.
--low-memory-unused
